@startuml
title Sequence Diagram – US 2.2.8 “Create and Submit Vessel Visit Notification”

actor "Shipping Agent Representative" as Agent
boundary "VesselVisitNotificationController\n(API Layer)" as Controller
control "VesselVisitNotificationService\n(Application Layer)" as Service
entity "VesselVisitNotificationRepository\n(Domain/Infrastructure)" as Repository
database "PortManagementContext (EF Core)\n(Infrastructure Layer)" as DB

note over Agent
User Story 2.2.8 – Create and Submit Vessel Visit Notification

"As a Shipping Agent Representative, I want to create and
submit a vessel visit notification, so that berthing and
(un)loading operations are scheduled in time."
end note

== Create Vessel Visit Notification ==

Agent -> Controller : POST /api/vesselvisitnotification\n(VesselVisitNotificationDTO)
activate Controller
Controller -> Service : CreateAsync(dto)
activate Service

note over Service
Validation Rules:
- VesselId and DockId must exist.
- Purpose determines if Cargo Manifests are required.
- Status initially set to "In Progress".
end note

Service -> Repository : AddAsync(VesselVisitNotification)
activate Repository
Repository -> DB : INSERT INTO VesselVisitNotifications (...)
DB --> Repository : OK
Repository --> Service : VesselVisitNotification persisted
deactivate Repository
Service --> Controller : VesselVisitNotificationDTO
deactivate Service
Controller --> Agent : 201 Created (VesselVisitNotificationDTO)
deactivate Controller

== Submit Vessel Visit Notification ==

Agent -> Controller : PUT /api/vesselvisitnotification/{id}/submit
activate Controller
Controller -> Service : SubmitAsync(id)
activate Service
Service -> Repository : GetByIdAsync(id)
activate Repository
Repository -> DB : SELECT * FROM VesselVisitNotifications WHERE Id = id
DB --> Repository : VesselVisitNotification (Status = InProgress)
Repository --> Service : VesselVisitNotification
deactivate Repository

note over Service
Business Rules:
- Only "In Progress" notifications can be submitted.
- Commercial visits must include at least one Cargo Manifest.
- Maintenance visits may omit manifests.
end note

Service -> Service : MarkAsSubmitted()
Service -> Repository : UpdateAsync(VesselVisitNotification)
activate Repository
Repository -> DB : UPDATE VesselVisitNotifications SET Status='Submitted'
DB --> Repository : OK
deactivate Repository
Service --> Controller : Success
deactivate Service
Controller --> Agent : 204 No Content
deactivate Controller
@enduml
